<main class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_320px] gap-10">
    <article>
  <% if(errors && errors.text) { %>
  <p class="text-red-500 text-sm mb-8"><%= errors.text %></p>
  <% } %>
  <% if(messages && messages.success) { %>
  <p class="text-green-500 text-sm mb-8"><%= messages.success %></p>
  <% } %>
      <!-- Breadcrumb -->
      <nav class="text-sm text-slate-500 mb-4 flex items-center gap-1.5">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-indigo-600">Home</a>
        <i data-lucide="chevron-right" class="w-3.5 h-3.5"></i>
        <a href="/categories/<%= post.category.slug %>" class="hover:text-indigo-600"
          ><%= post.category.title %></a
        >
        <i data-lucide="chevron-right" class="w-3.5 h-3.5"></i>
        <span class="text-slate-700 font-medium line-clamp-1"
          >
          <%= post.title %>
          </span
        >
      </nav>

      <span
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-xs font-semibold text-indigo-600 bg-indigo-50 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full mb-4"
      >
        <i data-lucide="tag" class="w-3 h-3"></i> <%= post.category.title %>
      </span>

      <h1
        class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 leading-tight mb-5"
      >
        <%= post.title %>
      </h1>

      <div
        class="flex items-center justify-between flex-wrap gap-4 mb-8 pb-6 border-b border-slate-200"
      >
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <img
            src="<%= post.author.avatar %>"
            class="w-11 h-11 rounded-full"
            alt="Author avatar"
          />
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-slate-800 text-sm"><%= post.author.username %></p>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">Aug 18, 2026 · 8 min read</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <button
            class="w-9 h-9 rounded-full border border-slate-200 flex items-center justify-center text-slate-500 hover:bg-slate-50"
            title="Like"
          >
            <i data-lucide="heart" class="w-4 h-4"></i>
          </button>
          <button
            class="w-9 h-9 rounded-full border border-slate-200 flex items-center justify-center text-slate-500 hover:bg-slate-50"
            title="Bookmark"
          >
            <i data-lucide="bookmark" class="w-4 h-4"></i>
          </button>
          <button
            class="w-9 h-9 rounded-full border border-slate-200 flex items-center justify-center text-slate-500 hover:bg-slate-50"
            title="Share"
          >
            <i data-lucide="share-2" class="w-4 h-4"></i>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div
        class="h-72 sm:h-96 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-br from-indigo-400 to-purple-500 flex items-center justify-center mb-10"
      >
        <!-- <i data-lucide="image" class="w-12 h-12 text-white/70"></i> -->
         <img src="<%= post.image %>" class="w-full h-full bg-center bg-contain rounded-md" alt="">
      </div>

      <div class="article-content">
        <%= post.text %>
        <!-- <p>
          Tailwind CSS has become the utility-first framework of choice for
          teams that want speed without sacrificing consistency. But as projects
          grow, so does the temptation to duplicate long class strings across
          dozens of components. This post walks through the patterns we use to
          keep things maintainable.
        </p>

        <h2>Start with design tokens, not colors</h2>
        <p>
          Rather than reaching for arbitrary hex values, define your palette in
          <code>tailwind.config.js</code> and reference semantic names like
          <code>primary</code> and <code>surface</code>. This makes global theme
          changes trivial and keeps your markup readable.
        </p>

        <blockquote>
          "A design system isn't a component library — it's a shared vocabulary
          between design and engineering."
        </blockquote>

        <h2>Extract components, not just classes</h2>
        <p>
          When a combination of utilities repeats more than twice, it's a signal
          to extract a component — not necessarily a CSS class. Using a
          component-based framework alongside Tailwind keeps logic and styling
          co-located while still avoiding duplication.
        </p>

        <h3>Common extraction candidates</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Buttons and button variants</li>
          <li>Form inputs and validation states</li>
          <li>Card layouts and list items</li>
          <li>Badges, tags, and status pills</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Keep your config lean</h2>
        <p>
          Resist the urge to add every possible utility variant. A focused
          <code>theme.extend</code> block is easier to reason about than an
          ever-growing list of one-off values scattered throughout the codebase.
        </p>

        <p>
          In the end, scalable Tailwind isn't about writing less CSS — it's
          about writing markup that stays predictable as your team and codebase
          grow.
        </p> -->
      </div>

      <!-- Tags -->
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mt-10 pt-6 border-t border-slate-200">
        <span class="text-sm text-slate-500 font-medium">Tags:</span>
        <a
          href="#"
          class="text-xs font-medium bg-slate-100 text-slate-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full hover:bg-slate-200"
          >tailwindcss</a
        >
        <a
          href="#"
          class="text-xs font-medium bg-slate-100 text-slate-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full hover:bg-slate-200"
          >css</a
        >
        <a
          href="#"
          class="text-xs font-medium bg-slate-100 text-slate-600 px-3 py-1 rounded-full hover:bg-slate-200"
          >design-systems</a
        >
      </div>

      <!-- Author card -->
      <div
        class="mt-10 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-6 flex items-center gap-4"
      >
        <img
          src="<%= post.author.avatar %>"
          class="w-16 h-16 rounded-full"
          alt="Author avatar"
        />
        <div>
          <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900"><%= post.author.username %></h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">
            Frontend engineer writing about design systems, CSS architecture,
            and developer experience.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Comments -->
      <section class="mt-12" id="comments">
        <h3
          class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-6 flex items-center gap-2"
        >
          <i data-lucide="message-circle" class="w-5 h-5 text-indigo-600"></i>
          Comments <span class="text-slate-400 font-normal">(3)</span>
        </h3>

        <!-- New comment form -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-5 mb-8">
          <div class="flex gap-3">
            <img
              src="<%= user && user.avatar ? user.avatar : "http://localhost:5500/uploads/images/users/profile.jpeg" %>"
              class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full shrink-0"
              alt="Your avatar"
            />
            <form action="/comments/<%= post.slug %>" method="POST" class="flex-1 space-y-3">
              <textarea
                name="text"
                rows="3"
                placeholder="Add a comment..."
                class="w-full px-4 py-3 border border-slate-200 rounded-lg text-sm focus:ring-2 focus:ring-indigo-500 focus:outline-none resize-none"
              ></textarea>
              <div class="flex justify-end">
                <button
                  type="submit"
                  class="px-5 py-2 bg-indigo-600 text-white text-sm font-semibold rounded-lg hover:bg-indigo-700 transition"
                >
                  Post Comment
                </button>
              </div>
            </form>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Comment list -->
        <div class="space-y-6">
        <% comments.forEach(comment => { %>
          <div class="flex gap-3">
            <img
              src="<%= comment.user.avatar %>"
              class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full shrink-0"
              alt="Commenter avatar"
            />
            <div
              class="flex-1 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-4"
            >
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-1.5">
                <span class="font-semibold text-sm text-slate-800"
                  ><%= comment.user.username %></span
                >
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-400">2 days ago</span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-600"><%= comment.text %></p>
              <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mt-3 text-xs text-slate-400">
                <button class="flex items-center gap-1 hover:text-indigo-600">
                  <i data-lucide="thumbs-up" class="w-3.5 h-3.5"></i> 4
                </button>
                <button class="hover:text-indigo-600">Reply</button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        <% }) %>

        </div>
      </section>
    </article>

    <!-- Sidebar -->
    <aside class="space-y-8">
      <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-6">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          <i data-lucide="list" class="w-4 h-4 text-indigo-600"></i> On this
          page
        </h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-500">
          <li>
            <a href="#" class="hover:text-indigo-600"
              >Start with design tokens</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="#" class="hover:text-indigo-600">Extract components</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="#" class="hover:text-indigo-600">Keep your config lean</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="#comments" class="hover:text-indigo-600">Comments</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-6">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          <i data-lucide="bookmark-check" class="w-4 h-4 text-indigo-600"></i>
          Related Posts
        </h3>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <a href="/post-detail" class="flex gap-3 group">
            <div
              class="w-14 h-14 rounded-lg bg-gradient-to-br from-sky-400 to-blue-500 shrink-0"
            ></div>
            <div>
              <h4
                class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-800 group-hover:text-indigo-600 line-clamp-2"
              >
                State Management in 2026: Do You Still Need Redux?
              </h4>
              <span class="text-xs text-slate-400">Aug 2, 2026</span>
            </div>
          </a>
          <a href="/post-detail" class="flex gap-3 group">
            <div
              class="w-14 h-14 rounded-lg bg-gradient-to-br from-rose-400 to-pink-500 shrink-0"
            ></div>
            <div>
              <h4
                class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-800 group-hover:text-indigo-600 line-clamp-2"
              >
                Accessible Color Systems for Modern Web Apps
              </h4>
              <span class="text-xs text-slate-400">Aug 6, 2026</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</main>
